#
# THE MUTANT IS THE CORRECT IMPLEMENTATION OF THE DROP CLAIM, which is what
# makes it worth planting. The claim is about the ANSWER a reader gets; the
# watermark is a PROMISE ABOUT A SEQUENCE, and Open re-derives that promise as
# the maximum largest_seq over the live tables because the manifest may not
# record a durable sequence (D7's forward binding).
#
# So a compaction free to drop the highest-sequenced entry -- a tombstone with
# nothing left to mask, exactly what the claim permits -- lowers that maximum,
# and DurableSeq goes BACKWARDS across a restart. Every answer is preserved and
# a promise is broken.
